XpdfWidget/Qt
=============

The XpdfWidget software and documentation are
copyright 2011-2019 Glyph & Cog, LLC.

Email: info@glyphandcog.com
WWW: http://www.glyphandcog.com/

The PDF data structures, operators, and specification are
documented in ISO 32000-1:2008.


------------------------------------------------------------------------
API DOCUMENTATION
------------------------------------------------------------------------

After unpacking the tar file, the API documentation will be located
in .../XpdfWidgetQtSrc-x.y.z/doc/index.html .


------------------------------------------------------------------------
INSTALLATION USING QMAKE
------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Unpack the tar file -- the following instructions will refer to
   the source directory (.../XpdfWidgetQtSrc-x.y.z) as $dir.

2. Copy the appropriate aconf-XXX.h file to aconf.h:
      Windows: copy aconf-win32.h aconf.h
      Linux:   cp aconf-linux.h aconf.h
      Mac:     cp aconf-mac.h aconf.h

3. Build FreeType, if needed.  The source can be downloaded from
   http://www.freetype.org/download.html and you can use the
   "misc/freetype.pro" file supplied with XpdfWidget to control the
   build.

4. Edit XpdfWidgetQt.pro and modify FREETYPE_INCLUDE_DIR and
   FREETYPE_LIB_DIR to point to the directories containing the
   FreeType headers and library.

5. Run qmake:

     qmake

6. Build:

     Windows:   nmake
     Linux/Mac: make

   That should leave the XpdfWidget library as:

     $dir/libXpdfWidget.a

7. To build the demo app, edit demo/XpdfWidgetQtDemo.pro, similarly to
   step #4.  Then run qmake and make:

     cd demo
     qmake
     make (or nmake)

   That should leave the demo executable as:

     $dir/demo/XpdfWidgetQtDemo


------------------------------------------------------------------------
QT QUICK / QML INTERFACE
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Building the Qt Quick / QML version of XpdfWidget is similar.  Follow
steps 1-3 above.  Then:

4. Rename "XpdfQuick.rename-to-pro" to "XpdfQuick.pro".

5. Edit XpdfQuick.pro and modify FREETYPE_INCLUDE_DIR and
   FREETYPE_LIB_DIR to point to the directories containing the
   FreeType headers and library.

6. Run qmake:

     qmake XpdfQuick.pro

7. Build:

     Windows:   nmake
     Linux/Mac: make

   That should leave the XpdfQuick library as:

     $dir/libXpdfQuick.a

8. To build the demo app, edit xpdf-qt/quick-demo/XpdfWidgetQtDemo.pro,
   similarly to step #5.  Then run qmake and make:

     cd xpdf-qt/quick-demo
     qmake
     make (or nmake)

   That should leave the demo executable as:

     $dir/xpdf-qt/quick-demo/XpdfQuickDemo
